WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.702
Tallyline is a self-hostable, open-source issue tracker where people and AI agents work the same board.

2
00:00:07.702 --> 00:00:11.425
Each project is a repo's worth of tickets and roadmap.

3
00:00:11.925 --> 00:00:15.754
Tickets move through one state machine, from triage to done.

4
00:00:15.754 --> 00:00:18.625
Here a person moves a card with the keyboard.

5
00:00:19.125 --> 00:00:23.460
An agent uses the same board through the Model Context Protocol.

6
00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.405
It asks what is ready, claims a ticket, comments, and moves it to review.

7
00:00:28.405 --> 00:00:33.350
The same rules apply, and the activity log records that the agent did it.

8
00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:40.525
The roadmap puts milestones and cycles on one timeline, with progress taken from the tickets themselves.

9
00:00:41.025 --> 00:00:49.025
The client overview has one row per project: status, progress, ticket counts, the next milestone and recent activity.

10
00:00:49.525 --> 00:00:55.604
Tallyline is AGPL-3.0, written in TypeScript, and runs on Docker and Postgres.

11
00:00:55.604 --> 00:00:57.475
You can run it yourself.
